        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 24 at 3:59PM PDT by NWS San Diego CA</headline>
        <description>At 359 PM PDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm over
San Jacinto, or 8 miles north of Hemet, moving northeast at 5 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects.

Locations impacted include...
Moreno Valley, Hemet, San Jacinto, southeastern Beaumont, East Hemet,
Juniper Springs, Homeland, Lakeview, Nuevo, Saboba Indian
Reservation, and Winchester.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.</instruction>
